                                <ECUC-PARAM-CONF-CONTAINER-DEF UUID="ECUC:58cabf39-0559-4574-8c5d-f10bb3c14862">
                                  <SHORT-NAME>EthSwtFilterMaxSduSizeEntry</SHORT-NAME>
                                  <DESC>
                                    <L-2 L="EN">EthSwtFilterMaxSduSizeEntry defines the maximum SDU size (size of an Ethernet packet) which is acceptable to be processed by the Ethernet switch.</L-2>
                                    <L-2 L="EN">Tags: atp.Status=draft</L-2>
                                  </DESC>
                                  <INTRODUCTION>
                                    <P>
                                      <L-1 L="EN">The value of EthSwtFilterMaxSduSizeEntry consider the size of the following parts of an Ethernet packet: * Preamble (7 byte) * SFD (start of frame delimiter) (1 byte) * Ethernet frame (Dst MAC,Src MAC, VLAN-tag, TypeField, Payload, CRC Checksum) * Minimum IPG (inter package gap) (12 byte times).</L-1>
                                    </P>
                                  </INTRODUCTION>
                                  <RELATED-TRACE-ITEM-REF BASE="ArTrace" DEST="TRACEABLE">ECUC_EthSwt_00224</RELATED-TRACE-ITEM-REF>
